<!-- Cosine palette explainer modal -->
<div class="shader-demo__help-modal shader-demo__help-modal--hidden" id="demo-cosine-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="About cosine palette">
  <div class="shader-demo__help-modal__backdrop" id="demo-cosine-backdrop"></div>
  <div class="shader-demo__help-modal__box">
    <div class="shader-demo__help-modal__header">
      <span class="shader-demo__help-modal__title">Cosine Palette</span>
      <button class="shader-demo__help-modal__close" id="demo-cosine-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    </div>
    <div class="shader-demo__help-modal__body">
      <p class="shader-demo__help-modal__intro">A cosine palette generates smooth, cyclical color progressions by oscillating each RGB channel independently using a cosine wave.</p>
      <p class="shader-demo__help-modal__formula"><code>color = A + B &middot; cos(2&pi;(C &middot; t + D))</code></p>
      <dl class="shader-demo__help-modal__defs">
        <dt>A &mdash; Palette A</dt>
        <dd>Brightness offset. Sets the center point that colors oscillate around.</dd>
        <dt>B &mdash; Palette B</dt>
        <dd>Amplitude. Controls the range of color swing — higher means more vivid output.</dd>
        <dt>C &mdash; Palette C</dt>
        <dd>Frequency. How many times the palette cycles across the gradient.</dd>
        <dt>D &mdash; Palette D</dt>
        <dd>Phase. Shifts the starting hue of the cycle.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

